<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Copy for the editor: canvas, widget list, inspector, background, styles, validate and
  install.

  Names are prefixed `editor_` because library-module resources merge into one table at the
  app level, where a bare name colliding with another module's would be silently overridden
  rather than reported. Two kinds of string deliberately stay in Kotlin:

  * decorative glyphs (⋯ ▦ ▧ ◫ ✓ ⇧ ← ↑ ↓ →) — symbols, not copy;
  * anything produced below the UI layer. Container diagnostics, validation errors and
    `WidgetGuide.supportMessage` come from :core:format and :core:model, which are
    framework-free by design and cannot reach a resource table; the same is true of
    :core:delivery's transfer messages. They arrive here as data and are rendered verbatim.
-->
